{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1727082","formula":"C₂₃H₂₄N₄O₆","hill":"C23H24N4O6","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":23.0,"H":24.0,"N":4.0,"O":6.0},"names":{"en":"Merimepodib"},"descriptions":{"en":"Merimepodib (VX-497) is a drug which acts as an inhibitor of the enzyme inosine monophosphate dehydrogenase, which is required for the synthesis of nucleotide bases containing guanine. This consequently inhibits synthesis of DNA and RNA, and results in antiviral and immunosuppressive effects. It progressed as far as Phase 2b human clinical trials against hepatitis C, but showed only modest benefits in comparison to existing treatments; however, it continued to be studied, and also shows activity against other viral diseases such as Zika virus and foot and mouth disease virus."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":153241,"mass":452.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=C(C=CC(=C1)NC(=O)NC2=CC=CC(=C2)CNC(=O)O[C@H]3CCOC3)C4=CN=CO4","inchikey":"JBPUGFODGPKTDW-SFHVURJKSA-N","iupac":"[(3S)-oxolan-3-yl] N-[[3-[[3-methoxy-4-(1,3-oxazol-5-yl)phenyl]carbamoylamino]phenyl]methyl]carbamate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"153241","atoms":57,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-5.39,"y":3.957,"z":-1.968,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.227,"y":2.126,"z":0.446,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.29,"y":1.32,"z":1.38,"el":"O"},{"x":3.879,"y":1.293,"z":1.44,"el":"O"},{"x":7.1,"y":0.577,"z":-0.992,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.091,"y":-1.007,"z":0.634,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.21,"y":0.024,"z":1.254,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.83,"y":-2.789,"z":-0.696,"el":"N"},{"x":1.382,"y":-2.133,"z":-0.791,"el":"N"},{"x":8.079,"y":1.661,"z":0.735,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.581,"y":3.367,"z":0.18,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.472,"y":3.167,"z":-0.823,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.538,"y":4.269,"z":-0.572,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.232,"y":3.128,"z":-2.134,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.463,"y":1.167,"z":1.059,"el":